    "q-139981": {
      "dom_id": "step-q139981",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider a $9\\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=4$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
