    "q-142481": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142481",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider a $4\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =4 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
