    "q-141232": {
      "dom_id": "step-q141232",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $A$ be a $6\\times 10$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=10,$ and since $B$ is formed by $4$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =10 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =10-4 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
