    "q-139982": {
      "dom_id": "step-q139982",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
